{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed bungalow dwelling would be at odds with the prevailing character of two storey dwellings within the local area. Furthermore, the proposed dwelling would have minimal separation to the eastern and southern site boundaries resulting in a cramped form of development that would appear as an overdevelopment of the constrained site. The proposal would be unacceptable in design terms contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposal would be in close proximity to the eastern side boundary and would sit 5m forward of the neighbouring property, 43a East Road resulting in a loss of light and a sense of enclosure for the occupiers of that property contrary to Local Plan policies CC1 and CC2.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposal does not include biodiversity or exception details. Without evidence to the contrary the proposal would result in harm to biodiversity contrary to London Plan policies G6 and G7 and Local Plan policy GB7.",
    "Reason : 4 - Without evidence to the contrary the proposal would fail to provide adequate surface water drainage contrary to London Plan SI 5 and Local Plan EQ3.",
    "Reason : 5 - Without evidence to the contrary the proposal would fail to make the fullest contribution to minimising carbon dioxide emissions contrary to London Plan policy SI 2 and Local Plan policy EQ1"
  ],
